  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "What is the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061x?$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's recall some of the basic properties of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061x:$\n\n- The domain of the function is $x\\in [-1,1].$\n\n- The range of the function is $y\\in [0,\\pi ].$\n\n- Its minimum value occurs at $x=1.$\n\n- Its maximum value occurs at $x=-1.$\n\n- Its $y$-intercept is $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\n- The function is strictly decreasing on its entire domain.\n\nOf the given functions, the only one that has all of these properties is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13962979/assets/d2677563c82c37fd1672a806a18524c97ea5ec17cb4f8ef6d8df23b827ba5e81.png)",
